.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-parhel-setup 1  "parhel 0.3.0" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git\-parhel\-setup \- Linux: create the store that gives filesystems without copy\-on\-write (ext4) cheap worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit parhel setup\fR [\fB\-\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-preallocate\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a per\-user btrfs image (the store) mounted at /parhel/<user> through a systemd mount unit, so `add` can create worktrees from sources on filesystems without copy\-on\-write, such as ext4. The worktree lives in the store and the requested destination becomes a symlink to it. Needs root (run it with sudo); the store belongs to the user who ran sudo, or to \-\-user (root is never inferred).
.PP
It creates, in order: /var/lib/parhel (root, mode 0700); the image /var/lib/parhel/<user>.img (sparse and 100G unless \-\-size, fully allocated with \-\-preallocate), formatted with mkfs.btrfs; the mount unit parhel\-<user>.mount in /etc/systemd/system, enabled and started, so the store comes back after a reboot; and, inside the mount, the user\*(Aqs directories and the .parhel\-store marker. Last, it sets the immutable attribute (chattr +i) on /var/lib/parhel, so that not even root can delete or rename an image by accident, and checks that it works. If it does not, the store stays usable and the command fails saying the image is not protected.
.PP
Safe to re\-run: a healthy store is left as it is, a stopped one is started, a missing protection is added. An image that holds a filesystem is never formatted. With \-\-remove the store is taken down: refused (store\-in\-use) while worktrees live in it, otherwise the unit, the image and the mount point are deleted.
.PP
The image is one file. Commits are safe in each repository\*(Aqs own .git, but uncommitted work in a store worktree is not: push what you cannot lose.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-size\fR \fI<size>\fR
Size of the store image: a number with an optional K, M, G or T suffix (default 100G, at least 256M). The image is sparse, so it takes disk space only as it fills
.TP
\fB\-\-preallocate\fR
Allocate the whole image now instead of letting it grow
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<name>\fR
Whose store to create (default: the user who ran sudo)
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
Take the store down: unmount, remove the unit and the image (refused while worktrees live in it)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  sudo git parhel setup
  sudo git parhel setup \-\-size 200G \-\-user alice
  sudo git parhel setup \-\-remove

Needs: mkfs.btrfs (btrfs\-progs), chattr (e2fsprogs), a kernel with btrfs, systemd.
Errors: not\-root, missing\-tool, unsupported\-platform, store\-in\-use, usage.
